Drops the wait a plan that appends nothing makes for the head entry its
outcome rests on (#672). Expected: NOT caught, reliably: the soak needs a
writer to retry a key in the microseconds between a failed flush's error
and its degrade; the nightly hit it at epoch 15 of one leg and 279 of
the other.
A 1,500 s run of this mutation (seed 40445801076, 349 epochs) passed. The
unit test below catches it every time.
Guarded-by: "pipeline: a del after a failed flush does not answer from the failed write before the degrade is published"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
index 184c7f5..1107f3b 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
@@ -410,7 +410,6 @@ auto DB::apply_batch(WriteOptions opts, WritePlan plan)
   if (opts.sync)
     last_synced_return = {instance_id_, std::chrono::steady_clock::now()};
 
-  settle_unappended(slot);
   return std::move(slot.result);
 }
 
